  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following statements about $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{O}_2$ is not correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\nIt is diamagnetic in nature\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nIt is derivative of $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}_2$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{O}_2$ oxidises $\\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}$ to $\\mathrm{CrO}_4^{2-}$ in acid medium.\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nIt is the super oxide of sodium",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{O}_2$ is peroxide of sodium not super oxide. The formula of sodium superoxide is $\\mathrm{NaO}_2$."
  }
